# --- [ Node ] ---
# Unanchored on purpose: this one legitimately appears at any depth, which is
# the case the unanchored form is actually for. Every pattern below that names
# one known directory at the repository root is anchored with a leading slash,
# because an unanchored pattern matches at *every* depth -- `storage/` once
# swallowed `src/storage/` and that module went uncommitted for weeks. See
# .agents/memory/decisions/gitignore-anchoring.md.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
.npm/

# --- [ Build output ] ---
/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- [ Test output ] ---
/coverage/

# --- [ Local environment ] ---
# .env carries secrets and a database URL and is never committed.
# wiki/environments/env.md documents every key it should hold.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- [ Local data ] ---
# The SQLite file the test and development profiles write to, and the
# artifact bytes the storage driver writes when it is backed by the disk.
#
# Anchored: unanchored, this also matched `src/storage/` -- the module that
# implements the driver -- and kept it out of the repository entirely.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
/storage/

# --- [ Editors ] ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# --- [ OS ] ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
